 ## Overview
-This method estimates the Unoriented Distance Field (UDF) value and the optimal direction $v^*$ at a query point $p$ by using a small SIREN network to generate $K_c$ candidate directions, computing associated distances and visibility, and aggregating them with softmax weights [S1]. It serves as the final step in the Viewshed Field pipeline, converting the Directed Distance Field (DDF) representation into a robust UDF estimate [S1]. Unlike computing $v^*$ via the gradient of the UDF (backward pass), which is noisier, this fitting approach provides a stable direction estimate by explicitly optimizing a set of candidate directions [S1].
